    "SQL-DEMAND"
  ],
  "description": "R-PAR-1 PAR-ERROR, SQL-DEMAND: Which error is reported first when three different bad rows exist (tx = 'x' at id 60 for CLng, zm = 0 at id 100 for the division, ov = 100000 at id 150 for CInt): SELECT id, CLng(tx), 1 / zm, CInt(ov) in id order, in id DESC order, without the CLng column, and with the columns in another order; nine GetRows(30) calls per statement record which call fails, with which error, and what the later calls give. Runs on a fresh copy of r-par-1-error opened read-only through DAO OpenDatabase in one process and one STA; each statement is opened with Database.OpenRecordset as a snapshot unless stated, and every call's result, HRESULT and DBEngine.Errors are captured.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
